<title>UK: IGC ups 96/97 Australia, EU, Argentina wheat sales.</title>
<headline>IGC ups 96/97 Australia, EU, Argentina wheat sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council on Thursday raised its forecasts for Australian, Argentine and EU 1996/97 wheat exports.</p>
<p>In its Grains Market Report it cut the estimate for Canadian wheat exports, while US exports were left unchanged.</p>
<p>The IGC put Australian exports at 14.5 million tonnes, compared with the previous forecast, made in November, of 13.5 million, and 12.1 million in 1995/96. It put Argentine exports at 10.0 million tonnes, compared with the previous forecast of 9.5 million and 4.4 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>EU exports were raised to 14.5 million tonnes, from the IGC's previous 14.0 and a 1995/96 performance of 12.6 million.</p>
<p>The forecast for US exports in 1996/97 was left at 25.5 million tonnes, down from 33.4 million last season.</p>
<p>The IGC puts total world wheat trade at 89.8 million tonnes, compared with the previous estimate of 88.5 million and 89.9 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
